# tiberius: the AVX-512 expert tier built with no VBMI in the translation unit, against upstream 146df3c4
# (v0.2.12, engine 0.1.58).
# REBASED 2026-11-08.  WHAT UPSTREAM NOW HAS ITSELF (PR 5120, commits f000d4a4 + 7e3fae57 in 0.2.12): the
# VBMI-free q2 unpack (expert.cpp's unpack64_q2_0_sw, selected at run time by cpu_vbmi_ok()), the split gates
# (cpu_vbmi_ok / cpu_vnni_ok / q2_rows_512_ok in expert_layout.{hpp,cpp}) and every call site that selects the
# VBMI-free rows through them.  It also makes the tier OPT-IN on a CPU without VBMI: cpu_vnni_ok() requires
# - any CPU with VBMI answers as before;
# - otherwise STRATA_VNNI_TIER=1 must be set (expert_layout.cpp), because on such a CPU the 512-bit rows round
#   differently from the AVX-2 rows it runs today.
# This box (Cascade Lake, VNNI, no VBMI) therefore gets the tier from the module's STRATA_VNNI_TIER=1
# (profiles/nixos/strata.nix), not from this patch.  The gate split, the gate renames and the call-site
# changes this patch used to carry are GONE - they were upstreamed, and carrying them here again would
# duplicate or shadow upstream's own probes.
#
# WHAT THIS PATCH IS NOW: the compile-time half of the same guarantee.  Upstream keeps -mavx512vbmi on
# expert.cpp and on iq_avx512.cpp/nvfp4_avx512.cpp and picks the VBMI-free forms at RUN TIME.  A run-time
# branch does not bound the COMPILER: in a TU built with -mavx512vbmi any function may receive VBMI code
# (the vectorizer's byte shuffles among them), and that is the SIGILL class this package already guards
# against.  So:
#   * expert.cpp: both 2-bit unpacks are made VBMI-free unconditionally, with tiberius's substitute
#     (VPERMW + VPSRLVW + VPMOVWB, byte-identical to VPMULTISHIFTQB, layout verified against a scalar
#     reference when written and deployed since the 0.1.x tier).  Upstream's run-time pair
#     (unpack64_q2_0_ms / unpack64_q2_0_sw + the cpu_vbmi_ok() branch) is replaced by that one form.
#   * CMakeLists.txt (root and sycl/): -mavx512vbmi removed from expert.cpp and from the
#     iq_avx512.cpp + nvfp4_avx512.cpp flag lists; KEPT on tq_avx512.cpp, which keeps cpu_avx512_ok().
#     iq_avx512.cpp and nvfp4_avx512.cpp hold no VBMI intrinsic (checked: no multishift / vpermb /
#     vperm2b / vpmadd52 / vpcompress / vpexpand in either file), so the flag removal cannot remove
#     something they need.
# The CONSEQUENCE the package asserts at build time (postPatch): expert.cpp contains no
# VPMULTISHIFTQB/multishift intrinsic, contains the VBMI-free shift form (_mm512_srlv_epi16), and neither
# expert.cpp nor iq/nvfp4_avx512.cpp carries -mavx512vbmi in either CMakeLists, while tq_avx512.cpp still
# does.  After editing the flag lists, objdump the built object:
#   objdump -d <expert.cpp.o> | grep -cE 'vpermb|vpermt2b|vpermi2b|vpmultishiftqb|vpmadd52|vpcompress|vpexpand'
# must be 0 (VBMI, VBMI2, IFMA).  cpu_vbmi_ok() is left in place (upstream's probe, now unused by this TU).
# NOT changed: expert.hpp's CpuFeatures::usable() still requires VBMI (upstream), which only the native
# Q2_0 pack's support path and the parity tool read - this lane's i-quant pack does not go through it.
#
# Measured on tiberius 2026-10-18 (ab18 campaign, 3 counterbalanced runs per arm): ~5% cheaper CPU expert
# pool+plan per decode window, GPU wait and Optane reads unchanged, outputs numerically sound (parity 0
# failures vs the ggml references) but NOT bit-identical to the AVX-2 tier on the long cells.
# See docs/exec-plans/active/tiberius-kernel-tuning.md.
#
# HISTORY: REBASED 2026-11-03 onto ffa80d73 and RE-VERIFIED 2026-11-05 onto c3b3f503 (then still carrying the
# gate split and the call-site hunks that 0.2.12 has since upstreamed).

